// BastiOS on AArch64: the kernel for QEMU's virt machine (make ARCH=aarch64).
//
// Platform: boot/aarch64 (entry, exception vectors, GICv3, the generic
// timer). Everything else is the kernel src/main.bastio runs on x86-64,
// proved under the same rules: the page allocator and address spaces, the
// process table and scheduler state, the file system, the system calls.
// What differs per architecture lives in src/aarch64/arch (the console
// device, registers, program images, the disk and the files the file system
// starts with).
//
// Not yet here: the Linux system-call layer (an arm64 ABI), the network and
// more than one processor. The user programs are the ones that need only
// the native calls (user/*.bastio built with `--target user --arch
// aarch64`): a program makes a call with `svc #0`, the number in x8 and the
// arguments in x0-x2 (bastiolang's user prelude), and gets the result in x0.

